^["architecture"]{
 # --- tokenizer bridge ---
 // spw-seed's lex() produces Token[] with {type, value, span: {start: {line, column, offset}, end}}
 // CM6 StreamLanguage expects token(stream, state) → string|null, character-by-character per line
 // bridge strategy: pre-tokenize → build line-indexed token map → wrap in StreamParser<State>
 // State = { lineTokens: Token[], tokenIndex: number }
 // token(stream, state): look up current position in lineTokens, advance stream, return token type string
 // re-tokenize on document change (full lex is fast for single-file sizes)

 #token_type_map: {
  // spw-seed Token.type → CM6 token type string (for StreamLanguage)
  OPERATOR: "operator",
  MODIFIER: "operator",
  CONNECTOR: "operator",
  CONTAINER_OPEN: "bracket",
  CONTAINER_CLOSE: "bracket",
  IDENTIFIER: "variableName",
  STRING: "string",
  NUMBER: "number",
  BOOLEAN: "bool",
  REFERENCE: "variableName.special",
  ANNOTATION: "meta",
  WHITESPACE: "",     // null — skip
  COMMENT: "comment",
  EOF: "",
  ERROR: "invalid",
 }

 # --- LSP bridge ---
 // child_process.spawn('node', ['path/to/stdio-server.js'])
 // JSON-RPC 2.0: { jsonrpc: "2.0", id, method, params } → { jsonrpc: "2.0", id, result }
 // notification (no id): initialize, textDocument/didOpen, textDocument/didChange
 // request (with id): spw/annotations, spw/contextAtPosition, spw/workspaceManifest, spw/workspaceTemperature
 // lifecycle: spawn on plugin load → initialize handshake → didOpen for vault .spw files → request/response loop → shutdown on unload

 # --- view architecture ---
 // ItemView subclass per view (ConceptsLeafView, AtlasLeafView)
 // registered via this.registerView(VIEW_TYPE, leaf => new View(leaf))
 // opened via app.workspace.getRightLeaf(false).setViewState({ type, active: true })
 // contentEl is a plain HTMLElement — build DOM with createElement, not React/Svelte
 // data flows: LSP request → parse response → build DOM tree → mount to contentEl
 // refresh: listen to vault events (modify, create, delete) → debounce → re-fetch → re-render

 # --- file view ---
 // TextFileView subclass for .spw extension
 // registerExtensions(['spw'], 'spw-file-view') in onload()
 // setViewData(data, clear): tokenize → render with syntax coloring → mount
 // getViewData(): return raw text (no round-trip corruption)
 // clear(): remove DOM children
 // this gives .spw files a dedicated viewer in Obsidian — click a .spw file, it opens with syntax highlighting

 # --- two rendering pipelines ---
 // 1. editing: CM6 registerEditorExtension → StreamLanguage adapter → live syntax in editor
 //    (only fires for .md files containing ```spw fences, since Obsidian editor is markdown-first)
 // 2. reading: registerMarkdownCodeBlockProcessor('spw', handler) → DOM nodes with token classes
 //    (fires in reading view / preview mode for ```spw fences)
 // 3. file: TextFileView subclass → .spw files opened directly
 //    (fires when user clicks a .spw file in the vault file explorer)
 // all three share spw-seed tokenizer; differ in output format (CM6 decoration / DOM / DOM)
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-04-05 00:00] observe — four interaction targets share a common surface: TextMate/Vim syntax, LSP client, custom request lane, views. Obsidian adds a fifth dimension: vault-native file topology
 >>[2026-04-05 00:01] observe — spw-seed has zero dependencies; bundles cleanly into any target
 >>[2026-04-05 00:02] observe — protocol types in vscode-spw/src/lsp/custom-requests.ts are portable interfaces wrapped in a vscode-specific client class. The interfaces can be extracted or duplicated
 >>[2026-04-05 00:03] decide — CM6 StreamLanguage wrapping spw-seed is the pragmatic path; defer Lezer grammar to a future branch
 >>[2026-04-05 00:04] decide — isDesktopOnly: true unlocks Node child_process for LSP subprocess; acceptable since Obsidian mobile has no .spw editing use case yet
 >>[2026-04-05 00:05] observe — Obsidian has two rendering modes: live editor (CM6) and reading view (post-processor). Plus a third: TextFileView for opening .spw files directly
 >>[2026-04-05 00:06] taste — the interaction-target pattern itself is a transferable abstraction worth distilling
 >>[2026-04-05 01:00] surprise — spw-seed tokenizer is token-array-based (full lex upfront), NOT character-streaming. CM6 StreamLanguage expects character-by-character token(stream, state). Need a bridge adapter: pre-tokenize → line-indexed map → position lookup. This is architecturally significant
 >>[2026-04-05 01:01] observe — spw-seed exposes lex() → Token[] where each Token has {type, value, span: {start: {line, column, offset}, end: {line, column, offset}}}. 24 token types. The span data is sufficient for line-indexed mapping
 >>[2026-04-05 01:02] observe — Obsidian overloads require() for @codemirror/* packages. Plugins MUST mark these as external in esbuild. Bundling a separate CM6 copy causes class identity mismatch and silent failures
 >>[2026-04-05 01:03] observe — Obsidian's Plugin class provides: addCommand, addRibbonIcon, addStatusBarItem, addSettingTab, registerView, registerExtensions, registerMarkdownCodeBlockProcessor, registerEditorExtension, registerEvent, registerDomEvent. All auto-cleanup on unload
 >>[2026-04-05 01:04] observe — VS Code concepts-tree.ts is 751 lines with co-occurrence graph, braid pairing, density bars, 4 grouping modes. The data model transfers; the tree node rendering needs Obsidian DOM adaptation
 >>[2026-04-05 01:05] observe — VS Code workspace-tree.ts is 741 lines with 9 node types, live cursor tracking (300ms debounce), spirit phase distribution, memory temperature tiers. Heavy LSP dependency: workspaceManifest, workspaceTemperature, contextAtPosition
 >>[2026-04-05 01:06] observe — annotation-index.ts maintains byName/byFile maps, rebuilds on file save (100ms debounce). Core schema: AnnotationEntry {uri, line, kind, name, sectionLabel?, framePath[]}. Transfers directly — the data shape is editor-agnostic
 >>[2026-04-05 01:07] observe — context-strip.ts renders "Spw: framePath > facets X | field A · B" in status bar with 80ms debounce. Direct analog: Obsidian addStatusBarItem() returns HTMLElement with setText()
 >>[2026-04-05 01:08] observe — semantics.ts is pure data: 23 sigils mapped to {role, physics, phase}. roots.ts: 27 sigil→path mappings with @here special case. Both transfer with zero adaptation
 >>[2026-04-05 01:09] decide — three rendering pipelines, not two: CM6 (editing fences), MarkdownCodeBlockProcessor (reading fences), TextFileView (direct .spw files). All share spw-seed tokenizer
 >>[2026-04-05 01:10] observe — Obsidian Vault API: read/cachedRead/modify/create/delete/rename/copy + getFileByPath/getAbstractFileByPath. All paths vault-relative. LSP uses file:// URIs. Bridge needs vault.adapter.getBasePath() to construct absolute paths for LSP
 >>[2026-04-05 01:11] observe — Obsidian events: vault.on('modify'/'create'/'delete'/'rename'), workspace.on('file-open'/'active-leaf-change'/'layout-change'). registerEvent() for auto-cleanup. MetadataCache.on('changed') for metadata-aware refresh
 >>[2026-04-05 01:12] observe — Obsidian CSS: plugin styles.css auto-loaded. CSS variables: --color-base-00 through -100, --accent-h/s/l, --font-text-size, --radius-s/m/l/xl. Valence pentad colors should use CSS custom properties layered on Obsidian's base theme
 >>[2026-04-05 01:13] taste — the token-map bridge pattern (pre-tokenize → line-index → position lookup) is reusable infrastructure. If spw-seed ever gets a Lezer grammar, the bridge can be swapped without changing the plugin's public surface
 >>[2026-04-05 01:14] decide — TextFileView for .spw files is the right first impression. A user with .spw files in their vault should be able to click one and see it rendered with full syntax coloring. This is the "durable" manifesto principle in action — the file format is future-proof and the tool adapts to it
 >>[2026-04-05 01:15] observe — the staff-level delta is no longer feature count; it is ownership of failure, restore, and proof surfaces. The branch needs explicit sidecars for CM6 substrate, runtime resilience, and validation evidence
 >>[2026-04-05 01:16] decide — create a distilled artifact (@artifact) rather than leaving all architectural truth trapped in PLAN.md and wip.spw. The branch introduces a real abstraction: vault-native interaction target
 >>[2026-04-05 01:17] observe — EditorSuggest and CM6 autocomplete are different planes. Future authoring assists may use both, but syntax and semantic rendering should not be routed through trigger-based suggestion APIs
 >>[2026-04-05 01:18] observe — a custom LSP bridge is only credible if the plan names restart policy, stale-state posture, workspace restore behavior, and user-visible health semantics before implementation
 >>[2026-04-05 01:19] decide — collect an evidence packet, not just build output: diagrams, timings, screenshots, failure drills, and manifesto traceability. This is application material as much as implementation guidance
 >>[2026-04-05 01:20] decide — scope Lezer as a separate portable parser package, not as code that lives inside obsidian-spw. The parser belongs to the language layer; the extension should consume it
 >>[2026-04-05 01:21] observe — the current seed parser's prose fallback, context-sensitive path sugar, and commit-style branches (?match, @_label) are the main reasons a direct seed→Lezer translation would sprawl or conflict
 >>[2026-04-05 01:22] decide — the first honest Lezer target is the strict symbolic Spw core for syntax trees, highlighting, and incremental reparsing. Replacing spw-seed semantics is a later equivalence project
 >>[2026-04-06 00:00] revise — removed self-conscious "staff signals" framing from PLAN.md and sidecars. The engineering should speak for itself; performative language undermines the design quality it claims to demonstrate
 >>[2026-04-06 00:01] implement — added risk_model and validation as optional frames in wip-template and wip convention. Updated plan schema and plan-template.md with Failure Modes and Validation sections
 >>[2026-04-06 00:02] implement — registered obsidian-spw, intellij-lsp4ij, neovim-spw-surfaces, commit-gate-redesign, lsp-custom-request-completions, vscode-plugin-performance, vscode-cognitive-surface, vscode-editor-contract in plan-ecology-clustering plan_map
 >>[2026-04-06 00:03] implement — added interaction_target_cluster and ecology_temperature frames to plan-ecology-clustering artifact. Added bridge rung to design_ladder
 >>[2026-04-06 00:04] taste — "interview_handles" renamed to "design_rationale" across sidecars. The questions are worth preserving; the frame name should describe what they are, not what they're for
 >>[2026-10-12 14:30] revise — Dormant plan, no extensions/obsidian-spw on disk, so no commit landed. Added a fence-scope probe as commit 2 (shifting the rest) so cm6_fence_scope is settled before the token adapter; added ?[protocol_types] from the taste debt; rewrote vault_uri and textfileview_editing as answerable questions (obsidian-api.spw:70 puts TextFileView under EditableFileView); one wonder added on fence activation.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:00] note — extensions/obsidian-spw does not exist yet, so files_hot names two paths not yet scaffolded; opened ?[hot_files_before_scaffold]; routed from lukewarm-backlog ?[obsidian_hot_unscaffolded].
 >>[2026-10-12 15:25] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 0 landed, 11 planned, 0 dropped.
 >>[2026-10-13 22:04] note — The parser release's reader variant (feature/reader-bundle) highlights Spw and outlines a file without a running server: roles, outline, anchors, and highlightHtml.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[vault_uri]: "Is vault.adapter.getBasePath() a stable public API, given the LSP needs file:// URIs built from vault-relative paths, or must the bridge take the vault root from a plugin setting?"
 ?[cm6_fence_scope]: "Does registerEditorExtension reach the contents of a spw fence inside a markdown note without extra language injection, and does ~[probe_fence_scope] decide it?"
 ?[textfileview_editing]: "obsidian-api.spw places TextFileView under EditableFileView, so is a TextFileView with an embedded CM6 EditorView enough for editing .spw files, or does editing need its own ItemView?"
 ?[workspace_restore]: "What minimum state do custom leaves persist via getState and setState so restore stays helpful but never stale-authoritative?"
 ?[completion_layer]: "If Spw completions ship later, which belong to EditorSuggest and which to CM6 or LSP completion, so authoring aids stay distinct from language semantics?"
 ?[lezer_boundary]: "Does the first Lezer grammar exclude prose fallback and context-sensitive path sugar so the parser stays structurally honest (lezer-parser-scope.spw leans yes)?"
 ?[lezer_markdown_activation]: "Even with a working Lezer package, which Obsidian or CM6 hook activates it for a spw fence in markdown editing?"
 ?[protocol_types]: "Are the portable custom-request interfaces in vscode-spw/src/lsp/custom-requests.ts extracted into a shared package or duplicated into the plugin, decided before the LSP manager commit?"
 ?[hot_files_before_scaffold]: "Should cache files_hot list extensions/obsidian-spw/src paths before ~[scaffold_plugin] scaffolds them (the directory does not exist yet), or only the plan files until then? Tracked at ~"../lukewarm-backlog/wip.spw" ?[obsidian_hot_unscaffolded]."
}

